 "ledger_total": 2531,
 "method": "Every approved policy exception and what happened after it (worst stage, max DPD, default, rating drift over the four quarters after the decision, read from the book), and loss and migration rates by exception type against non-exception peers. Peers are risk-matched: the expected rate for an exception type is the non-exception rate in each rating band, weighted by the type's own band mix, so a type that is simply given to weaker borrowers is not blamed for their rating. Rates carry 95% Wilson intervals and n; observed/expected carries a Poisson interval. Verdict per type: tighten (O/E interval above 1 and n >= 30), watch (O/E >= 1.25 or n < 30), keep.",
 "data_note": "Decision history is a fictional seed published to Data Domains (domain governance, gov_* relations, ops/r13_seed_governance.py); outcomes (stage, DPD, default, rating drift) are the corporate book's own."
}